# martenot — one held note, and the TOUCHE ridden all the way up and back down.
# The A/B seed for Part 51's loudness→brightness tricks (audit §F7, plan item 1.7).
#
# The whole claim is about a RELATIONSHIP — brightness tracking loudness — so a static note proves
# nothing and a struck note proves less. This holds one pitch and sweeps only the intensity, which is
# the single variable the three modes disagree about:
#   filter  cutoff rides intens^2 (as shipped)   · morph  cutoff parked open, the WAVE dulls
#   gate    volume constant, cutoff IS the gate
#
# 'A' is the bottom keybed key (GarageBand musical typing) and is HELD for the whole clip: with a key
# down, `pitchPtr` is set and the intensity target follows the touche `lever`, which UP/DOWN ride at
# 0.025 per frame — so ~40 held frames covers the full 0..1 travel.
#
#   node tools/ab-render.js martenot --set loud_mode=MODE_FILTER,MODE_MORPH,MODE_GATE \
#        --script tools/clips/martenot/01-touche-swell.script --frames 240
#   node tools/wav-envelope.js <wav> 100    # amplitude vs CENTROID: do they rise and fall together?
#
# In MODE_GATE the amplitude curve should stay flat-ish while the centroid sweeps, since there the
# filter is doing the gating instead of the VCA. That is the tell.
down 5 a
down 15 UP
up 60 UP
down 100 DOWN
up 150 DOWN
up 200 a
